    "summary": "Ventura ’82 bursts with a smoking Truckin’ and a rare Playing→China Cat→Dark Star jam.",
    "review": "The July‑17, 1982 Ventura County Fairgrounds show is pure summer heat turned up to eleven. The first set rolls along with a tight Bertha opening, but the real fireworks come on the back half – Tennessee Jed and a monster Truckin' that ends the set in high gear. The second set is where this night truly shines: a blazing Playing In The Band segues into an unforgettable China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider, then launches into a rare Playing > China Cat > Dark Star sequence that feels both spacey and deeply melodic. Highlights like The Wheel and the late‑night wrap‑up with One More Saturday Night keep the momentum roaring, while the encore’s gentle “It’s All Over Now Baby Blue” offers a sweet cool‑down.\n\nFrom an audio standpoint the front‑of‑house matrix capture (gd1982-07-17.fob.nak300.ho.bowen-foster.102172.flac) is the gold standard – crystal‑clear, instrument‑balanced and immersive enough to feel you’re right in the fairgrounds breezy crowd. Audience tapes also do a solid job of conveying the venue’s ocean‑air vibe, but they can’t match the matrix’s detail. For anyone looking to relive a high‑energy early‑’80s Dead night with standout jams and superb sound, this Ventura show is a must‑listen.",
